  "evidence_interpretation": [
    "Rebuilt ignored validator wrapper from frozen current production sources; full persistent gate and every current build-input hash independently rechecked.",
    "Recursively checked 1202 unique file/hash bindings,85 JSON files,566 raw command streams across43 reports. Fifteen negative reports match declared outcomes; exactly one deliberate hang has its expected watchdog timeout.",
    "Final build PE bytes repeat the retained 60000-mutation and268-truncation probe results:37363 accepted plans satisfy checked reservation/run/fixup invariants;22905 rejected inputs remain contained.156 reserved bootstrap mutations and70 final serial mutations rejected.",
    "Eight weakened evidence variants all rejected: weaker phase, missing reference, wrong reference hash, optional host test, missing Windows scenario, absent reference comparison, missing private disk and weakened markers.",
    "Windows and Door run the identical independent MSVC/MASM EXE. Its final exit73 follows nonvolatile register checks; output alone is insufficient. Private P08 disk hashes remain identical before and after Windows execution."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "Finite code review and tests do not prove absence of every bug.",
    "P09 qualifies one bounded no-CRT single-thread Windows console fixture on declared QEMU q35/TCG profile. Arbitrary Windows applications, physical hardware and Windows SMP/thread behavior are not qualified.",
    "DLL initialization, Windows TLS lifecycle, exception dispatch/unwind, CRT and broader file/async/Unicode behavior remain P10 or later; compiler exception helper fails closed.",
    "Output memory stability relies on enforced single-thread/no-heap personality; revisit before adding Windows threads. ASCII writes are limited to1024 bytes and original compatibility exports are a documented subset.",
    "Existing P08 development capability authentication and native text-console limitations remain. No GUI milestone or universal compatibility claim follows.",
    "Hashes establish identity within the trusted local workspace rather than external attestation."
  ],
